  "body": "Found by the release QA swarm (#2582) on **v0.24.0**. Common tools a user asked for are missing from `list_tool_catalog`, so each run had to copy another entry and edit diameter, shank and feeds by hand (easy to get wrong):\n\n- **Ø3 ball end mill** (`add_tool {catalog:\"BN-0300\"}` -> `no catalog tool named 'BN-0300'`); balls are only Ø6 and Ø10. No Ø6 bull nose (only Ø10 R1).\n- **Metric jobber drills** for tap drills and clearance holes: only DR-0200/0300/0400/0600, so no Ø5.0 (M6 tap drill) or Ø6.6 (M6 clearance).\n- Spot drill: see #897 (no spot-drill kind). Threading inserts for M16x1.5: see #893.\n\nRun reports: skull `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/REPORT.md` (P1), len `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q02-3d-mold/REPORT.md` (problem 4).\n\nDone means: the catalog carries a Ø3 ball, a Ø6 bull nose and the metric tap-drill / clearance drill sizes for M3-M12 (with feeds), and `add_tool` picks them by name.\n",
